<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Status</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>status
status skills
status weapons
status spells
</pre>
<p>Shows your lasting qualities, where <a cmd='#'>score</a> shows how you are doing right 
now.
</p><p>Status alone shows:
</p>
<ul><li>your title, your guilds and your profession;</li>
<li>your abilities: strength, dexterity, constitution, charisma, brain, magic, divine and hit points, with your hit points now and at most;</li>
<li>your combat dexterity: your dexterity as your armour leaves it (heavy armour slows you down);</li>
<li>the skill and ability points you have left to practice with (see <a cmd='#'>Help Practice</a>);</li>
<li>whether you are brave or wimpy (see <a cmd='#'>Help Wimpy</a>), and your speed in a fight, when it isn't the normal one.</li></ul>
<p>Status skills, status weapons and status spells list how well you know 
each skill, weapon and spell you have learned; spells are split into those 
of magic and those of divine power. You can shorten them: status sk, 
status w, status sp.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Score</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Abilities</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Practice</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Guilds</a>
</pre>




</div>